# Prose and hand-maintained config.
#
# Prettier owns code — TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON. It does not own the prose, and
# the line is drawn deliberately rather than by omission:
#
#   * Markdown here uses meaningful line breaks, aligned tables and callouts written
#     to a 100-column budget. Reflowing them produces large diffs that say nothing,
#     and PRD.md / PED.md are transcriptions where fidelity to the source matters.
#   * YAML here is read by tools (TASKS.yaml, budget.yaml, usage-model.yaml) and by
#     people deciding whether a gate is right. Its shape is part of its argument.
#
# The docs are not ungated: links, anchors and line endings are all checked by
# `make verify`. They are just not reformatted.
*.md
*.yaml
*.yml

# Deliberately ill-formed; they exist to prove the gates are not vacuous.
tools/toolchain-smoke/fixtures/

# Generated by tools/gen_kics_queries.js. Prettier collapses short arrays and
# JSON.stringify never will, so formatting these would fight the generator every run
# and leave the --check gate permanently stale. The generator owns their shape.
security/kics-queries/zero-cost/

# The oracle's frozen outputs, where the bytes ARE the contract (CORE-01).
#
# This one is not a preference. `make verify` asserts that tools/oracle-py reproduces
# these files byte for byte, so anything that reformats them breaks the freeze — and
# Prettier wants to, because it wraps a long string where json.dumps does not. Two
# tools cannot both own these bytes; the generator owns them, and the whole point of
# the file is that nothing reformats it quietly.
golden/oracle/

# Generated by `pnpm -C packages/contracts schema`, and compared byte for byte against
# the generator's own output. Prettier formats JSON differently from
# JSON.stringify(_, null, 2), so letting it touch this file makes the staleness check
# fail every time the file is correct.
packages/contracts/schemas/
